---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ukgaap/frs105.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Micro-entity Size Thresholds" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Simplified Recognition and Measurement" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Fixed Asset Investments and Investment Property — Cost, Not Fair Value" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Minimal Mandatory Disclosure Notes" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Filing Simplifications — Filleted and Abridged Accounts" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Confirming Micro-entity Eligibility" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Investment Property at Cost, Not Fair Value" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s11", label: "FRS 105 vs FRS 102 vs IFRS — Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The lightest-touch tier of the entire UK GAAP hierarchy</div><div class="principle">FRS 105 exists to provide the SMALLEST qualifying UK/Irish companies — "MICRO-ENTITIES" — with a genuinely SIMPLIFIED accounting and disclosure regime, reflecting that the COST and COMPLEXITY of full FRS 102 compliance can be disproportionate for very small businesses with limited external users of their accounts. It sits at the BOTTOM of the FRS 100 decision tree — a further step DOWN in complexity even from FRS 102's own Section 1A small-entity relief.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Micro-entity Size Thresholds</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Meeting at least two of three Companies Act size criteria</div><div class="principle">A company QUALIFIES as a micro-entity if it meets AT LEAST TWO of the following THREE thresholds (subject to periodic UK statutory updates): TURNOVER not more than approximately £632,000; BALANCE SHEET total (gross assets) not more than approximately £316,000; and an AVERAGE of not more than 10 EMPLOYEES during the financial year. Certain entities (e.g. public companies, most financial institutions, charities) are EXCLUDED from the micro-entities regime REGARDLESS of size.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Simplified Recognition and Measurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A deliberately minimal, prescriptive set of accounting choices</div><div class="principle">FRS 105 SIMPLIFIES recognition and measurement RELATIVE to FRS 102 in several ways: it does NOT offer the fair value ACCOUNTING OPTIONS available under FRS 102 for certain assets (Section 4); deferred TAX is recognised on a SIMPLIFIED basis; and OVERALL, FRS 105 removes many of the ELECTIVE policy choices FRS 102 offers, presenting micro-entities with a more PRESCRIBED, less judgement-intensive set of requirements.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Fixed Asset Investments and Investment Property — Cost, Not Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A notable simplification relative to FRS 102's fair value option</div><div class="principle">Under FRS 102, INVESTMENT PROPERTY is generally measured at FAIR VALUE through profit or loss (a genuinely different treatment from ordinary owner-occupied property). Under FRS 105, however, investment property (and fixed asset investments generally) are measured SIMPLY at COST LESS DEPRECIATION and any IMPAIRMENT — WITHOUT the fair value remeasurement option FRS 102 provides. This is a DELIBERATE simplification, sparing micro-entities the COST and JUDGEMENT burden of obtaining regular fair value assessments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Minimal Mandatory Disclosure Notes</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Only a small number of specific footnote disclosures are required</div><div class="principle">FRS 105 requires only a SMALL, SPECIFIC set of mandatory notes — broadly, guarantees/commitments not otherwise recognised, advances/credits to directors, and financial support/off-balance-sheet arrangements — a DRAMATICALLY reduced disclosure burden compared to even FRS 102's Section 1A small-entity regime, reflecting the assumption that micro-entity accounts serve a NARROWER range of external users.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Filing Simplifications — Filleted and Abridged Accounts</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reduced public filing requirements at Companies House</div><div class="principle">Micro-entities preparing accounts under FRS 105 may take advantage of FURTHER Companies Act FILING simplifications — for example, filing only a Balance Sheet (with limited notes) at Companies House, WITHOUT the Profit and Loss Account or Directors' Report being made PUBLICLY available — reflecting a policy balance between transparency and the PROPORTIONATE administrative burden appropriate for very small companies.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Confirming Micro-entity Eligibility</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Meeting two of three thresholds</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A small consultancy company</div><div class="wk-body">A consultancy has turnover of £480,000, a balance sheet total of £210,000, and an average of 6 employees during the year.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company meets ALL THREE thresholds (turnover under £632,000; balance sheet total under £316,000; employees under 10) — comfortably qualifying as a <strong>MICRO-ENTITY</strong>, and may elect to prepare its accounts under <strong>FRS 105</strong> instead of the fuller FRS 102 (with or without Section 1A relief).</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Investment Property at Cost, Not Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Foregoing FRS 102's fair value option</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A micro-entity holding a rental property</div><div class="wk-body">A micro-entity holds an investment property purchased for £250,000, with a current market value of £310,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Under FRS 105, the property remains at its <strong>£250,000 COST</strong> (less any depreciation and impairment) — the entity CANNOT elect to remeasure it to the £310,000 FAIR VALUE, unlike an equivalent entity reporting under FULL FRS 102, which would generally measure investment property at fair value through profit or loss.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What FRS 105 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>A statement that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with the micro-entities regime</span><span>Guarantees, commitments, and contingencies not otherwise recognised</span><span>Advances and credits granted to directors</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether the entity meets the micro-entity size thresholds and is not otherwise excluded from the regime</span><span>Whether to elect FRS 105 if eligible, versus remaining on FRS 102</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — FRS 105's prescriptive, simplified approach limits the scope for significant estimation</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>FRS 105 vs FRS 102 vs IFRS — Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — FRS 105 vs FRS 102 vs full IFRS</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">FRS 105</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">FRS 102 / Full IFRS</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Investment property</span><span>Cost less depreciation/impairment ONLY</span><span>Fair value option available (FRS 102) / IAS 40 fair value or cost model choice (IFRS)</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Accounting policy elections</span><span>Minimal — largely prescribed</span><span>Multiple genuine policy choices available (development costs, borrowing costs under FRS 102)</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Mandatory disclosure notes</span><span>Very limited, specific set only</span><span>Considerably more extensive</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">FRS 105 is genuinely the SIMPLEST tier of the entire UK GAAP hierarchy — deliberately trading away flexibility and disclosure depth in exchange for PROPORTIONATE simplicity for the smallest companies.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every FRS 105 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Investment property</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS / SOFP</span></span><span>Held at cost less depreciation/impairment, not fair value</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Filing at Companies House</span><span>Public record</span><span>May be limited to a Balance Sheet with minimal notes</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>FRS 100</span><span>Directs eligible micro-entities toward FRS 105 within the overall UK GAAP hierarchy</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>FRS 102</span><span>The standard a micro-entity would otherwise apply if not electing FRS 105</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Micro-entity</div><div class="glossary-def">A company meeting at least two of three Companies Act size thresholds (turnover, balance sheet total, employee numbers), eligible for the FRS 105 simplified regime.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Filleted accounts</div><div class="glossary-def">A simplified filing option allowing certain statements (e.g. the Profit and Loss Account) to be omitted from the publicly filed version of a small company's or micro-entity's accounts.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.frs105 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
